  "doc.title": "How a Computer Boots · a long essay you can play with",
  "doc.desc": "About a dozen seconds pass between pressing the power button and the login screen. How does a CPU that knows nothing find its first instruction, its memory, its disk and the operating system, and how does it make sure what it loads is not malicious? Ten hands-on models: ATX power-on timing, the reset-vector address, how long an SPI flash read takes, where boot time goes, an ACPI table checksum, the GUID partition table with CRC32, the Secure Boot signature chain, the cost of revoking a signed boot loader, TPM PCR extends, and how long it takes to wake the other cores.",
  "nav.back": "← Knowledge index",
  "nav.lang": "Language",
  "toc.label": "Contents",
  "toc.title": "Contents",

