  "footer": "How a Computer Boots · a long essay you can play with. Models: ATX power-on timing (Intel, ATX Version 3 Multi-Rail Desktop Platform Power Supply Design Guide, revision 2.1a, 2023, tables 4-2 and 4-10); the x86 reset vector and multiprocessor initialization (Intel 64 and IA-32 Architectures Software Developer's Manual, Volume 3, order number 325384-093US, September 2026, sections 12.1.4, 11.4 and 12.8.5); SPI flash read commands (Winbond W25Q256JV datasheet, revision I, 2018); ACPI table headers and MADT (ACPI specification, following edk2's Acpi10.h and Acpi65.h); GUID partition table and CRC32 (UEFI specification, Chapter 5, following edk2's UefiGpt.h, UefiMultiPhase.h and Mbr.h); SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4) and textbook RSA signatures; signature database entry sizes (edk2 ImageAuthentication.h); SBAT (rhboot/shim's SBAT.md); PCR extension (TPM 2.0 Library Specification, Part 1, revision 1.59, section 17.2); core wake-up time (Thomas Gleixner, Linux patch notes, 4 May 2023). Sources, dates and anything not verified are listed in this directory's BRIEF.md."
